e-consuming. <span style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">This guide will show you how to save design elements and layouts for reuse</span>, helping you maintain symmetry and consistency in your emails.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">By following these tips, you can streamline your email creation process and ensure your emails always look polished and well-structured. Let's dive in!<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><u style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">I</strong><strong style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">n t</strong></u><strong style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\"><u dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">his Article, find the guide to:</u></strong></p><p data-identifyelement=\"470\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 20px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Arial, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">1. Save elements/ sections or layouts<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">2. Rename these sections for better administration<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">3. Search the items for quick access</p><p data-identifyelement=\"470\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Arial, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing: bord